.TH ISOFORGE 1 "2026-09-01" "isoforge 2.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
isoforge \- downloads Linux images, writes them to USB (single image or Ventoy multi-ISO), and builds custom installable ISOs from a recipe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B isoforge
[build ...] [--config PATH] [--version] [--help]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Isoforge downloads Linux images, writes them to USB (single image or Ventoy multi-ISO), and builds custom installable ISOs from a recipe.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B build [ARGS]
Build a custom ISO from a recipe. Pass --help for its options.
.TP
.B --config PATH
Override config file path.
.TP
.B --version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/isoforge/config.json
Default configuration when installed system-wide.
.TP
.I $HOME/Downloads/iso_images
Default download directory used when the \fBdownload_dir\fR configuration option is missing or empty.
